\section{Exception Handling and Fault Management}
\subsection{Division-by-Zero Prevention}
Reciprocal mass caching prevents:
\begin{itemize}
    \item divide-by-zero faults,
    \item sign-flip instability,
    \item runaway numerical divergence.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Topology Fault Isolation}
Corrupted topology vectors are sandboxed and isolated from the main solver 
pipeline. Faults are logged and corrected via encrypted coordinate keys.

\section{Conclusion}
This systems-engineering validation suite defines the complete verification 
framework for exotic-matter astrodynamics and topological metric simulation. 
The suite ensures that all modules satisfy analytical physics constraints, 
numerical stability requirements, robustness criteria, and metric-tensor 
integrity standards.